{560}{}{For years, the war raged on and was considered a victory for us. However, no matter how many troops fell to our superior technology, the NCR always seemed to have more replacements available. The Brotherhood, on the other hand, wasn't so fortunate.}
{561}{}{How come?}
{562}{}{No?}

{590}{}{As an elitist group, replacements were scarce. It became obvious that we were doomed to lose the war due to the NCR's overwhelming numbers. Morale at the bunker began to falter as the war seemed more and more hopeless. Eventually, it happened. Lower-ranking members of the Brotherhood began deserting their posts.}
{591}{}{We're going through tough times right now, but the Brotherhood will prevail! Just as it did before. Farewell, Brother.}
{592}{}{We crush NCR bad guys! Bye-bye now.}
{593}{}{But what exactly started it all?}
{594}{}{Why war?}

{620}{}{You're asking about old ghosts there, kid. The Brotherhood-NCR war... well, that's a story steeped in bad blood and old grudges. I suppose it was inevitable. The NCR was always hungry, always expanding. They just wanted to spread, control, and consolidate power. But the Brotherhood... we've always been about preserving the old world, not making a new one. We kept the technology of the old world safe, kept it out of the hands of those who'd misuse it.}
{621}{}{And that led to war?}
{622}{}{Then war?}

{650}{}{Well, there's a bit more to it than that. You see, the real trouble started with the assassination of President Tandi in 2248 and the bombing of the NCR Congress the following year. Ah, those dark days. Yeah, they shook the wasteland, no doubt about it.}
{651}{}{What can you tell me about President Tandi?}
{652}{}{Prez Tadi?}

{680}{}{Tandi... she was a force of nature, a visionary. She turned Shady Sands from a small, struggling settlement into the backbone of the New California Republic. But not everyone saw her dream of a unified wasteland as a good thing.}
{681}{}{So, she was assassinated?}
{682}{}{Tadi die?}

{710}{}{That's right, though the details are murky. Some say it was a lone gunman, others claim a conspiracy within the NCR. There were even whispers about Enclave remnants or even the Brotherhood being involved, but there's never been any concrete proof. Her death left a vacuum, and chaos followed.}
{711}{}{And the bombing of the Congress?}
{712}{}{Boom?}

{740}{}{That happened not long after Tandi's assassination. The NCR Congress was in session when the bombs went off. It was a massacre. It sent a shockwave throughout the NCR, destabilizing their government for quite a while.}
{741}{}{Who was behind the bombing?}
{742}{}{Who boom?}

{770}{}{That's been a subject of debate for years. Official NCR reports claim it was the work of Brotherhood extremists, because of a plasma bomb used for it, but we deny it. There's always been speculation about other groups too - the Khans, the Enclave, even internal factions within the NCR. Whoever did it, it pushed the NCR and the Brotherhood further apart, fueling the fire of war.}
{771}{}{Fascinating. Thanks for answering my questions. Farewell.}
{772}{}{Wow! Bye-bye.}

{800}{}{Brother, we face a dire situation.}
{801}{}{Sister, we face a dire situation.}
{802}{}{Devon, in his betrayal, has changed all the access codes to our bunker's armory. All our supplies have been tampered with. Without weapons and armor, we are vulnerable.}
{803}{}{That's a significant security breach, Elder. We need to act swiftly.}

{830}{}{Agreed. We have reason to believe that Isaac Gant, a former Brotherhood member, possesses knowledge of the reset codes. Your task is to track him down and retrieve these codes by any means necessary.}
